//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_REQ_REALTIME", overlay = false)

// ⭐⭐ THE REALTIME HALF OF REQUEST ALIGNMENT — the one measurement in this
// programme that CANNOT BE TAKEN AT THE WEEKEND.
//
// `pineRuntimeFrontend`'s request path refuses `lookahead` by name and says
// exactly why:
//
//     Vendor packet M1 measured the HISTORICAL half of this alignment on a real
//     chart; the realtime half needs an open market and is still owed. Serving
//     lookahead on a guess would put a number on screen that nobody could have
//     traded on — the most valuable-LOOKING wrong answer available.
//
// ⭐ AND THE SCOPE NARROWED ON 2026-09-23. A request for the chart's OWN symbol
// at the chart's OWN period now folds to the expression, because there is no
// period to be part-way through — so `lookahead` is inert there and needs no
// measurement at all. What remains owed is ONLY the case this probe asks: a
// requested timeframe genuinely ABOVE the chart's, on a bar that is still
// forming.
//
// ⛔⛔ RUN IT ON AN INTRADAY CHART DURING REGULAR HOURS. On a daily chart the
// requested 'D' IS the chart's period and every channel below collapses to the
// identity — the probe would return a clean, meaningless row. **5m on SPY,
// between 09:30 and 16:00 ET, with the newest bar forming.**
//
// ⛔ A FAILED STUDY KEEPS A ONE-PLOT STUB with an EMPTY `_data._items`, so
// assert `isFailed === false` before reading the roster. See
// `exchange-spelling.pine`, which learned that from an identifier that does not
// exist in Pine v6.

// ── the two readings whose DIFFERENCE is the whole question ─────────────────
// ⭐ SAME CALL, SAME SYMBOL, SAME TIMEFRAME — only the merge strategy differs.
// Anything else varying between them would make the delta unreadable.
dOn  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
dOff = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

plot(dOn,  "R1_close_D_lookahead_ON")
plot(dOff, "R2_close_D_lookahead_OFF")

// ⭐⭐ R3 IS THE MEASUREMENT. On a HISTORICAL bar the two must agree (packet M1
// measured that half). On the FORMING bar they are expected to diverge — and by
// how much, in which direction, is precisely what has never been read.
// ⛔ A DIFFERENCE, NOT TWO NUMBERS: reading R1 and R2 separately invites
// comparing values captured a tick apart.
plot(dOn - dOff, "R3_DELTA_on_minus_off")

// ⭐ R4/R5 SAY WHICH BARS THOSE WERE. Without them a non-zero R3 cannot be
// attributed to the realtime bar rather than to a stale historical one, and the
// whole capture becomes a shrug.
plot(barstate.isrealtime ? 1 : 0, "R4_isrealtime")
plot(barstate.islast     ? 1 : 0, "R5_islast")

// ⭐⭐ R6 IS THE ANCHOR THE DELTA IS JUDGED AGAINST. `lookahead_on` at a HIGHER
// timeframe is expected to return the value of the daily bar CURRENTLY forming —
// which on the last bar should equal this chart's own `close`. If R1 equals R6
// on a realtime bar, the merge is reading the in-progress period; if R2 equals
// the PREVIOUS daily close instead, that is the non-repainting half.
plot(close, "R6_chart_close")

// ⭐ R7 — the previous completed daily close, so "off returns the last CLOSED
// period" can be checked directly rather than inferred from a difference.
plot(request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close[1],
     lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off), "R7_prev_D_close_OFF")

// ⛔ R8 IS THE NON-VACUITY CONTROL AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. Every channel above
// can legitimately read 0 — a zero delta is in fact the EXPECTED historical
// answer — so "the two strategies agree" and "the study never evaluated" are
// otherwise the same row. `bar_index` is never constant on a chart with bars, so
// a flat R8 means the probe is broken and the whole row must be discarded.
plot(bar_index, "R8_bar_index_CONTROL")

// ── how to run it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⛔ FOLLOW `docs/pine/capture-procedure.md`, and read the VALUES from
// `study._data._items` — never a screenshot. A pixel cannot carry a delta.
//
// ⚠️ THE LAST BAR IS THE ONLY ROW THAT ANSWERS. Capture the whole series, then
// read the row where R5 (`islast`) is 1 and R4 (`isrealtime`) is 1. Every other
// row is the historical half, which is already measured — those rows are the
// probe's own control that it agrees with packet M1.
//
// WITNESS
//     SPY, 5m, regular hours, newest bar forming.
//
// ⭐ ONE SYMBOL IS ENOUGH HERE, and that is a real difference from the syminfo
// roster: the question is about the MERGE STRATEGY, which is a property of the
// request, not of the instrument. A second symbol would repeat the reading
// rather than widen it.
//
// RECORDING — name the invocation so the next reader can reproduce the row
// rather than trust it, and record the ET timestamp of the capture: this is the
// one reading whose meaning depends on the market being open when it was taken.
//
//     "_invocation": "tools/visual_conformance/probes/request-realtime-alignment.pine
//                     pasted into the TradingView editor on SPY 5m during RTH;
//                     plot values read from study._data._items per
//                     docs/pine/capture-procedure.md"
